window.DOCS_EN={"示例": "Examples", "文档": "Documentation", "安装 ↗": "Install ↗", "菜单": "Menu", "跳到正文": "Skip to content", "主导航": "Main navigation", "Journey 首页": "Journey home", "切换语言": "Switch language", "走进故事": "Enter the story", "实际示例": "Live examples", "使用指南": "Documentation", "给 coding agent 的用户旅程地图 · Journey Skill": "Customer journey maps for coding agents · Journey Skill", "Agent 懂代码。": "Your agent knows your code.", "懂用户吗？": "Does it know your users?", "代码在 repo 里，agent 读得到。人的体验不在。": "Your code is in the repo, where your agent can read it. Your users' experience isn't.", "Journey 把它记成 .journey/ 里的一张旅程地图，放在代码旁边。": "Journey keeps it as a journey map in .journey/, right next to your code.", "聊着就能建，需求变了按 diff 改，证据和猜测分开标。": "Build it by talking, update it by diff, and keep evidence apart from guesses.", "安装 Journey ↗": "Install Journey ↗", "看它如何工作 ↗": "See how it works ↗", "为什么需要它？": "Why does it matter?", "进入六幕粒子故事": "A six-act particle story", "滚动体验": "Scroll through", "暂停粒子动画": "Pause particle animation", "播放粒子动画": "Play particle animation", "▶ 动态": "▶ Motion", "Ⅱ 暂停": "Ⅱ Pause", "说清楚场景。": "Describe the situation.", "地图交给 Journey。": "Journey builds the map.", "不用先学字段，也不用选模板。": "No fields to learn, no template to pick.", "从你手头的一段经历、访谈或产品笔记开始。": "Start from an experience, an interview or product notes you already have.", "把对话整理成地图": "Turn a conversation into a map", "“梳理用户第一次申请这份工作的经历。”": "“Map what it's like to apply for this job for the first time.”", "按里程碑和步骤建立结构，连接人的目标、行为、情绪与触点。留下可继续编辑的旅程文件。": "Builds milestones and steps that connect people's goals, actions, feelings and touchpoints, and leaves a journey file you can keep editing.", "改需求，接着改地图": "Requirements change, the map follows", "“现在允许跳过注册，会影响哪些步骤？”": "“We now let people skip sign-up. Which steps does that affect?”", "修改相关步骤与引用，记录改了什么、为什么改。下一次对话从已有地图继续。": "Updates the affected steps and references and records what changed and why. The next conversation picks up from the same map.", "同一份理解，交给不同的人": "One understanding, for different readers", "“给评审会一张地图，给工程师一份交接。”": "“A map for the review, a handoff for the engineers.”", "从同一份旅程生成交互视图、简报、故事线或规格说明，按读者需要组织信息。": "Turns one journey into interactive views, a brief, a storyline or a spec, organised for each reader.", "看得到步骤。": "See every step.", "也查得到判断的来处。": "And where each judgment came from.", "下方直接读取仓库的求职示例。": "The map below reads the skill's job-application example directly.", "15 个步骤、分支与字段都可以逐项检查。": "All 15 steps, branches and fields can be inspected one by one.", "打开地图，查看原始字段 ↗": "Open the map and inspect raw fields ↗", "断点说明：AI 筛选未记录情绪，不代表中性或零分。": "About the gap: the AI screen has no recorded emotion. That doesn't mean neutral or zero.", "横向看阶段，纵向看体验 · 点击打开完整地图": "Stages across, experience down · click to open the full map", "在项目里，持续保存": "Saved in your project", "Markdown 旅程保存在 .journey/，能进版本控制，也能在后续会话里接着用。": "The Markdown journey lives in .journey/. It can be versioned and picked up in later sessions.", "把推断和依据分开": "Inference kept apart from evidence", "来源标记保留判断来处。缺少依据的内容，可以被找到、追问和补充。": "Provenance markers keep track of where a judgment came from. Claims without evidence can be found, questioned and backed up.", "修改前后，有迹可循": "Every change is traceable", "脚本写入前检查结构与引用，变更记录保留操作与备注。": "The script checks structure and references before writing; the change log keeps each operation and note.", "测试通过了。": "The tests passed.", "人为什么还在门外？": "So why are people still outside the door?", "一条提前十五分钟预订的规则，一间空着的会议室。跟着两个人走一遍，看看需求遗漏了什么。": "A rule that rooms must be booked 15 minutes ahead, and an empty meeting room. Follow two people through it and see what the requirement missed.", "进入故事": "Enter the story", "从建立地图，": "From building the map", "到持续维护。": "to keeping it current.", "了解完整工作方式 ↗": "See the full workflow ↗", "从人的目标，": "Start from", "开始。": "people's goals.", "把对话里的目标、行为和触点整理成旅程。": "Turn the goals, actions and touchpoints from a conversation into a journey.", "看见薄弱处，": "Find the weak spots,", "再向前。": "then move on.", "检查痛点与缺失信息，发现值得继续梳理的旅程。": "Check pain points and missing information, and find journeys worth mapping next.", "改动局部，": "Change a part,", "保留全貌。": "keep the whole.", "按步骤修改，让新的理解留在原有上下文里。": "Edit step by step, so new understanding stays in its context.", "改坏的地图，": "A broken map", "存不进去。": "won't save.", "写入前校验结构和引用，出错就拦下。": "Structure and references are validated before writing; errors are stopped.", "让判断，": "Every judgment", "有据可查。": "has a source.", "追溯字段来源，区分观察、人工修改与推断。": "Trace where fields came from: observation, human edit or inference.", "每次修改，": "Every change", "留下记录。": "leaves a record.", "查询修改内容、作者与备注，保留决策轨迹。": "Query what changed, who changed it and why, and keep the decision trail.", "同一份地图，": "One map,", "换一种视角。": "other perspectives.", "从时间、情绪、协作和依据等角度理解旅程。": "Read the journey through time, emotion, collaboration and evidence.", "让下一位，": "Hand it on", "接得住。": "cleanly.", "把旅程转成简报、故事线或工程交接。": "Turn the journey into a brief, a storyline or an engineering handoff.", "装进你的 agent，": "Install it in your agent,", "从一句话开始。": "start with one sentence.", "“帮我梳理新用户第一次使用产品的旅程，": "“Map a new user's first experience with our product,", "把你不确定的地方标出来。”": "and mark anything you're unsure about.”", "阅读快速开始 ↗": "Read the quick start ↗", "用户旅程地图概览：四个阶段与六个体验维度": "Journey map overview: four stages and six experience dimensions", "当前路径的情绪曲线；AI 筛选未记录情绪，曲线在此断开": "Emotion curve for the current path; the AI screen has no recorded emotion, so the curve breaks there", "推门即用 · Journey 故事": "Walk In · Journey story", "推门即用，六幕沉浸式故事": "Walk In, an immersive story in six acts", "推门即用 · 六幕粒子故事": "Walk In · a six-act particle story", "一条规则。一个被遗漏的人。": "One rule. One person it missed.", "正在进入故事…": "Entering the story…", "独立打开故事 ↗": "Open the story on its own ↗", "退出故事": "Exit story", "退出故事，返回原位置": "Exit the story and return to where you were", "故事载入较慢，可以退出后重试，或独立打开。": "The story is slow to load. Exit and try again, or open it on its own.", "示例 · Journey Skill": "Examples · Journey Skill", "同一份旅程。": "One journey.", "看见不同的问题。": "Different questions.", "每个视图，都从一个具体问题出发。打开示例，检查步骤、时间和依据，也看看它们是如何被表达出来的。": "Each view starts from a concrete question. Open an example to inspect its steps, timing and evidence, and how they are expressed.", "十五分钟，": "Fifteen minutes —", "是怎么消失的？": "where did they go?", "对照修改前后的会议室旅程，逐步查看情绪、等待和来源标记。这里接续故事，也能独立阅读。": "Compare the meeting-room journey before and after the change, step by step: emotion, waiting and provenance. It continues the story, and stands on its own.", "打开交互案例 ↗": "Open the interactive example ↗", "探索这个视图 ↗": "Explore this view ↗", "用户旅程图": "Journey map", "按阶段对照行为、想法、触点、情绪、痛点与机会。": "Compare actions, thoughts, touchpoints, emotion, pain points and opportunities by stage.", "时长条形图": "Duration bars", "比较各步骤的时长；无法量化的等待保留原文。": "Compare how long each step takes; waits that can't be quantified keep their original wording.", "角色矩阵图": "Role matrix", "按角色和步骤交叉查看参与关系。": "See who takes part in which step.", "字段矩阵图": "Field matrix", "查看字段是否记录，以及是否带有来源标记。": "See which fields are recorded and which carry provenance markers.", "故事板": "Storyboard", "按步骤展开行为、角色和当事人的想法。": "Unfold actions, roles and the person's thoughts step by step.", "流程图": "Flow graph", "按阶段查看完整流程，以及筛选和回复时的分支。": "See the whole flow by stage, including the branches at screening and reply.", "卡片网格": "Card grid", "按里程碑查看全部步骤，打开卡片检查原始字段。": "See every step by milestone and open a card to inspect its raw fields.", "泳道画布": "Swimlane canvas", "缩放与拖动，对照用户行为、前台、后台和支持系统。": "Zoom and drag to compare user actions, frontstage, backstage and support systems.", "时长比例图": "Time to scale", "使用线性刻度比较真实时长，保留无法量化的等待。": "Compare real durations on a linear scale, keeping waits that can't be quantified.", "九个视图都由本站根据 skill 自带的求职示例旅程（demos/gallery/job-application-portal.md）绘制，不是 skill 的原样输出。标 TEMPLATE 的视图对应 skill 的同名渲染模板，由本站重新实现；标 CUSTOM LAYOUT 的视图 skill 没有自带模板，可以让 agent 按需搭建。流程图缩略图按阶段汇总，打开后可查看全部步骤与分支。示例数据不代表真实用户研究。": "All nine views are drawn by this site from the skill's example journey (demos/gallery/job-application-portal.md); they are not the skill's output as-is. Views marked TEMPLATE re-implement the skill's rendering template of the same name; views marked CUSTOM LAYOUT have no template in the skill and can be built by the agent on request. The flow-graph thumbnail is summarised by stage; open it for every step and branch. The example data is not real user research.", "同一份旅程。你的表达方式。": "One journey. Your way of showing it.", "选择布局、组合交互，再用主题统一视觉。查看 skill 实际使用的模板和命令。": "Pick a layout, combine an interaction and unify it with a theme. See the templates and commands the skill actually uses.", "制作模板与切换主题 ↗": "Make templates and switch themes ↗", "图表主题": "Chart theme", "emotionValence 原始数值；横轴为文件中的步骤顺序，缺失值保留断点": "Raw emotionValence values; the x-axis follows step order in the file, and missing values leave a gap", "时间记录：可量化时长按对数刻度呈现；不确定时长保留原文": "Time records: quantifiable durations on a log scale; uncertain durations keep their original wording", "角色协作矩阵，根据每步 persona 字段绘制": "Role matrix, drawn from each step's persona field", "PERSONA × STEP · 实心点表示该步骤记录了这个角色": "PERSONA × STEP · a filled dot means the step records this role", "13 个常用字段的记录矩阵；空框表示未记录，小圆点表示带来源标记": "Coverage of 13 common fields; an empty box means not recorded, a small dot means a provenance marker", "故事板：每一帧使用步骤 description 与 persona 原文": "Storyboard: each frame uses the step's original description and persona", "由实际里程碑汇总的流程概览；打开后查看完整步骤与分支": "Flow overview summarised by milestone; open it for every step and branch", "卡片网格，前六个步骤预览": "Card grid, previewing the first six steps", "服务蓝图：用户行为、前台行动、后台行动、支持系统；未记录处保留为空": "Service blueprint: user actions, frontstage, backstage and support systems; unrecorded cells stay empty", "线性时长比例图：0–24 小时，各行独立，未知等待不虚构为数值": "Linear time-to-scale chart: 0–24 hours, each row independent; unknown waits are not turned into numbers", "用户行为": "User actions", "前台行动": "Frontstage", "后台行动": "Backstage", "支持系统": "Support systems", "未记录": "Not recorded", "未定量": "Not quantified", "求职旅程 · Journey Skill": "Job application · Journey Skill", "Maya 的求职旅程": "Maya's job application", "一位在职求职者，从发现职位到收到结果。先读完整旅程，再切换视角看时间、协作和分支。": "A job seeker with a job, from finding a posting to getting an answer. Read the whole journey first, then switch views to see time, collaboration and branches.", "视图": "View", "图表视角": "Chart view", "示例视图": "Example views", "横向看阶段，纵向看人的经历。切换结局，查看不同路径。": "Stages across, the person's experience down. Switch the ending to see different paths.", "在职求职者 · 通过线上门户申请工作": "Employed job seeker · applying through an online portal", "目标": "Goal", "申请一份适合自己的工作，获得明确的后续回应。": "Apply for a job that fits and get a clear answer back.", "查看路径": "Path", "阶段": "Stage", "想法": "Thoughts", "触点": "Touchpoints", "痛点": "Pain points", "机会": "Opportunity", "行为": "Action", "情绪": "Emotion", "未记录想法": "No thought recorded", "未记录痛点": "No pain point recorded", "未记录机会": "No opportunity recorded", "未记录触点": "No touchpoint recorded", "情绪未记录": "Emotion not recorded", "+2 积极": "+2 positive", "0 中性": "0 neutral", "−2 消极": "−2 negative", "阶段内展示关键字段的中文摘要；点击内容可检查原文。空白项保留为未记录。": "Each stage shows the key fields; click to inspect the original. Blank cells stay unrecorded.", "情绪数值来自 emotionValence；没有记录的值保留断点。点击步骤可检查原始字段。": "Emotion values come from emotionValence; unrecorded values leave a gap. Click a step to inspect its raw fields.", "点击图中步骤，展开详情": "Click a step in the chart for details", "步骤详情": "Step details", "选择图中任一步骤": "Pick any step in the chart", "选择左侧步骤，查看它的原始字段。": "Pick a step on the left to see its raw fields.", "查看原始数据": "View raw data", "完整 JSON 与字段说明": "Full JSON and field notes", "这张图的数据": "Data behind this chart", "job-application.json · 15 个源步骤": "job-application.json · 15 source steps", "复制 JSON": "Copy JSON", "已复制": "Copied", "已选中，请复制": "Selected — copy the text", "复制": "Copy", "下载 JSON ↓": "Download JSON ↓", "图表与详情读取同一份数据。": "The chart and the details read the same data.", "查阅字段定义 ↗": "Field definitions ↗", "用在我的项目里": "Use it in my project", "生成模板、复用主题": "Make templates, reuse themes", "先生成自己的地图。": "Start with your own map.", "选择布局与交互，拿走可交给 agent 的提示词。": "Pick a layout and an interaction and take away a prompt for your agent.", "制作我的模板 ↗": "Make my template ↗", "给已有 HTML 应用当前主题": "Apply this theme to existing HTML", "来源：skill 自带的求职示例旅程（demos/gallery/job-application-portal.md），用于演示；不代表真实用户研究。未记录的字段保留为空。九个视图都由本站绘制：标 TEMPLATE 的对应 skill 同名渲染模板，由本站重新实现；标 CUSTOM LAYOUT 的 skill 没有自带模板，可以让 agent 按需搭建。": "Source: the skill's example journey (demos/gallery/job-application-portal.md), for demonstration; not real user research. Unrecorded fields stay empty. All nine views are drawn by this site: TEMPLATE views re-implement the skill's rendering template of the same name; CUSTOM LAYOUT views have no template in the skill and can be built by the agent on request.", "用户旅程地图，可横向滚动": "Journey map, scrolls horizontally", "选择旅程步骤": "Pick a journey step", "原始旅程数据": "Raw journey data", "JSON 原始数据": "Raw JSON", "其他原始字段": "Other raw fields", "时间花在了哪里？": "Where does the time go?", "明确的数值按对数刻度绘制。范围用粗线，未定量的等待保留原文。": "Explicit values are drawn on a log scale. Ranges are thick lines; unquantified waits keep their wording.", "刻度为秒 / 分钟 / 小时 / 天；每行是单步时长，不是累计时间。≤ 表示上限。": "The scale runs seconds / minutes / hours / days; each row is one step, not a running total. ≤ marks an upper bound.", "一个步骤，牵动哪些角色？": "Who does each step involve?", "角色直接来自 persona 字段。点击一列，在原文里继续查看交接与前后台工作。": "Roles come straight from the persona field. Click a column to read handoffs and front- and backstage work in the original.", "实心点 = 该步骤中记录了此角色 · 点的大小不代表工作量。": "Filled dot = the step records this role · dot size is not workload.", "记录了什么，还缺少什么？": "What's recorded, and what's missing?", "检查 13 个常用字段。实心方块表示有记录，空框表示没有记录。": "Checks 13 common fields. A filled square is recorded; an empty box is not.", "小圆点 = 有来源标记。本例只有两个 backstage 字段标记 auto-composite；其余未标记，不能据此认定为事实。": "Small dot = provenance marker. In this example only two backstage fields are marked auto-composite; the rest are unmarked and shouldn't be taken as fact.", "跟着 Maya，重新走一遍。": "Walk it again with Maya.", "每一帧展示 description 和 persona 原文；选择后可阅读完整行为与想法。": "Each frame shows the original description and persona; select one to read its full actions and thoughts.", "编号与源文件顺序一致。结局包含多个分支。": "Numbers follow the source file order. The ending has several branches.", "流程图 · 从发现职位到结果": "Flow graph · from posting to outcome", "连接只来自 next 字段。AI 筛选与最终回复分别形成分支；进入面试指向另一张地图。": "Links come only from next fields. The AI screen and the final reply each branch; the interview leads to another map.", "按四个里程碑排列的流程图；所有连线来自 next 字段": "Flow graph laid out by the four milestones; every link comes from a next field", "不匹配": "No match", "匹配": "Match", "拒绝": "Rejected", "推进面试": "Advance to interview", "面试旅程 ↗": "Interview journey ↗", "箭头来自 next 引用 · 分支标签为中文译文，选中节点可查看原始条件。": "Arrows come from next references · branch labels are summaries; select a node to see the original condition.", "卡片网格 · 每一步都能展开检查": "Card grid · every step can be opened", "按里程碑组织全部 15 个步骤。卡片保留原始描述，点击后读取完整字段。": "All 15 steps grouped by milestone. Cards keep the original description; click to read every field.", "… 点击读完整字段": "… click to read every field", "内容直接来自旅程数据；不同结局作为独立步骤保留。": "Content comes straight from the journey data; each ending stays a separate step.", "时长比例图 · 等待有多长？": "Time to scale · how long is the wait?", "使用 0–24 小时的线性刻度，保留原文中的范围、近似值与上限。未知等待单独标记。": "A linear 0–24 hour scale that keeps the ranges, approximations and upper bounds from the original. Unknown waits are marked separately.", "每行独立，不可相加为总旅程。虚线框表示上限；短任务可能细至不足一个像素，这正是实际比例。": "Rows are independent and don't add up to a total. Dashed boxes are upper bounds; short tasks can be thinner than a pixel — that is the real proportion.", "服务蓝图 · 一张可以探索的画布": "Service blueprint · a canvas to explore", "从用户行为向下看前台、后台与系统。缩放和拖动，在全貌与局部之间切换。": "Read down from user actions to frontstage, backstage and systems. Zoom and drag between the whole and the detail.", "各层直接读取对应字段，未记录处不会自动推断。方向键平移，＋ / − 缩放，0 查看全图。": "Each lane reads its own field; nothing is inferred where a field is missing. Arrow keys pan, + / − zoom, 0 shows everything.", "拖动画布 · Ctrl / ⌘ + 滚轮缩放": "Drag the canvas · Ctrl / ⌘ + scroll to zoom", "全图": "Fit", "放大画布": "Zoom in", "缩小画布": "Zoom out", "可缩放泳道图：方向键平移，加减键缩放，0 查看全图": "Zoomable swimlane: arrow keys pan, + and − zoom, 0 shows everything", "发现职位": "Discover the job", "提交申请": "Apply", "筛选与等待": "Screening and waiting", "收到结果": "Outcome", "看到职位": "See the posting", "判断是否适合": "Assess fit", "点击申请": "Click apply", "创建账户": "Create an account", "填写申请": "Fill in the form", "收到确认": "Get confirmation", "AI 筛选": "AI screen", "快速拒绝": "Fast rejection", "等待消息": "Wait in silence", "查询与跟进": "Check status / follow up", "收到回复": "Hear back", "被拒绝": "Rejection", "没有下文": "Ghosted", "进入面试": "Advance to interview", "收到拒信": "Rejection letter", "始终无回复": "Never hear back", "筛选后快速拒绝": "Fast rejection after screening", "Maya 的用户旅程地图：阶段、行为、想法、触点、情绪、痛点与机会": "Maya's journey map: stages, actions, thoughts, touchpoints, emotion, pain points and opportunities", "会议室旅程 · Journey Skill": "Meeting room · Journey Skill", "从门外，走进去。": "From outside the door, to inside.", "切换方案，再点击一个步骤。查看局部修改如何影响等待时间、人的感受和后续行动。": "Switch versions, then click a step to see how a local change affects waiting time, how people feel and what they do next.", "修改前 · 提前预订": "Before · book ahead", "修改后 · 推门即用": "After · walk in", "旅程版本": "Journey version", "旅程情绪曲线": "Journey emotion curve", "想聊一下": "Need to talk", "提前预订": "Book ahead", "找到房间": "Find a room", "一起讨论": "Talk it through", "离开房间": "Leave the room", "感受": "Feeling", "等待": "Wait", "关键时刻": "Moment of truth", "下一步": "Next", "来源标记 · 示例设定": "Provenance · part of the scenario", "改动，也留下记录。": "The change leaves a record, too.", "删除提前预订步骤，修正后续引用，再更新找到房间的行为和感受。原始文件与变更记录都可以查看。": "Remove the book-ahead step, fix the references after it, then update how finding a room goes and feels. The original files and the change log are all available.", "修改前 ↓": "Before ↓", "修改后 ↓": "After ↓", "变更记录 ↓": "Change log ↓", "有来源标记，也要检查依据。": "A provenance marker still needs checking.", "本案例的观察、次数和指标均为叙事设定。来源标记让判断可追溯；结构校验负责检查地图是否完整，不替代真实的用户研究。": "The observations, counts and metrics in this case are part of the story. Provenance makes judgments traceable; structural validation checks the map is complete. Neither replaces real user research.", "回到完整故事 ↗": "Back to the full story ↗", "和同事在工位讨论一个 bug，三句话说不清，决定\"找个房间画一下\"": "Discussing a bug with a colleague at their desks; three sentences in, they decide to \"find a room and draw it\"", "急，想马上说清楚": "Impatient, wants to sort it out now", "现在就去，五分钟就够": "Let's go now, five minutes is enough", "讨论卡住，需要白板": "The discussion is stuck and needs a whiteboard", "每人每周 3–4 次": "3–4 times per person per week", "61% 的会议在发起后 10 分钟内开始": "61% of meetings start within 10 minutes of being called", "source: 门禁 + 日历记录，3 周": "source: badge + calendar logs, 3 weeks", "打开预订系统，规则要求至少提前 15 分钟预订": "Opens the booking system; the rule says to book at least 15 minutes ahead", "不耐烦": "Impatient", "手机日历": "Phone calendar", "必须提前 15 分钟预订，杜绝占用": "Rooms must be booked 15 minutes ahead, to stop squatting", "走到一间空会议室门口，灯没开，门口屏显示\"请于 15 分钟后使用\"": "Walks up to an empty meeting room, lights off; the door screen says \"Available in 15 minutes\"", "荒唐，憋气": "Absurd, frustrated", "房间就在眼前，空的，我要在门口等它？": "The room is right here and empty, and I have to wait outside?", "会议室门口": "Outside the meeting room", "门口屏": "Door screen", "15 分钟": "15 minutes", "空房间就在眼前，却不能用": "An empty room right there, and you can't use it", "规则在防占用，挡住的却是正在需要它的人": "The rule is meant to stop squatting, but it blocks the people who need the room", "放弃，站在走廊讨论；或订一个\"幽灵会议\"长期占房": "Give up and talk in the hallway, or book a \"ghost meeting\" to hold the room", "每天早上先把下午的房间全订上": "Book every afternoon room first thing in the morning", "source: 走廊观察 2 天，23 次": "source: hallway observation, 2 days, 23 times", "在白板上画了二十分钟，问题说清楚了": "Twenty minutes at the whiteboard and the problem is clear", "顺了": "Relieved", "~20 分钟": "~20 minutes", "提前散会，预订还剩 40 分钟，房间空着，别人订不到": "They finish early with 40 minutes left on the booking; the room sits empty and nobody else can book it", "无感": "Indifferent", "预订制本身制造了空占": "Booking itself creates idle rooms", "54% 的预订提前结束，平均空置 31 分钟": "54% of bookings end early, leaving the room empty for 31 minutes on average", "source: 门口传感器，2 周": "source: door sensor, 2 weeks", "走到一间空会议室门口，门口屏亮着\"空闲\"，推门即用；预订变成可选，只有想提前锁房才需要": "Walks up to an empty meeting room; the door screen shows \"Free\" and they walk in. Booking is optional, only for holding a room ahead of time", "顺，几乎没注意到这一步": "Smooth, barely noticed the step", "空着，进。": "Empty. In.", "空房间就在眼前，推门就能用": "An empty room right there, and you just walk in", "门口传感器 10 分钟无人，自动释放房间": "The door sensor releases the room after 10 empty minutes", "小林": "Lin", "预订系统": "Booking system", "门口传感器": "Door sensor", "[小林]": "[Lin]", "[小林, 预订系统]": "[Lin, Booking system]", "[预订系统]": "[Booking system]", "[预订系统, 门口传感器]": "[Booking system, Door sensor]", "全部": "All", "字段": "Field", "下载": "Download", "深色阅读": "Dark reading", "纸白阅读": "Light reading", "“大部分要求都符合，但不是全部。值得花时间申请吗？”": "\"I hit most of these, but not all — is it worth my time?\"", "职位要求模糊或过高，难以判断是否适合。": "Vague or inflated requirements make it hard to judge fit", "区分必须满足的条件与加分项。": "Mark which requirements are actually firm and which are wish-list", "“这份工作可能适合我，先看看要求。”": "\"This could actually be a good fit — let me see what they want\"", "还没看到申请表，就必须先注册账户。": "Account gate before she's even seen the form", "允许先申请，提交时再注册；或支持访客申请。": "Let people apply first and create the account at submit — or offer a guest apply", "上传了简历，还要重复填写；解析出错后要手动修正。": "\"I just uploaded my resume — why am I typing it all again?\" · Parser mangles formatting, she fixes it by hand", "只解析一次，让申请人确认，避免重复填写相同信息。": "Parse once, show it back for confirmation, never ask for the same fact twice", "“有人看过申请吗？要不要跟进，又怕打扰他们。”": "\"Did anyone even look at it? Did I do something wrong? Should I follow up or will that annoy them?\"", "不知道是否有人看过，没有状态、时间线或明确结果。": "No acknowledgment that a human ever reviewed it · No status, no timeline, no closure", "展示真实的内部进度，例如正在审核、通常需要两周。": "Surface the real internal state, even coarsely — \"in recruiter review, typically ~2 weeks\"", "自动回复没有说明下一步或时间安排。": "A generic auto-reply with no sense of timeline or next steps", "告诉申请人接下来会发生什么，以及预计时间。": "Say what happens next and by when — the cheapest fix in the whole journey", "“至少知道结果了，但真的有人看过吗？”": "\"At least I know now — but did a person ever actually look at this?\"", "没有不匹配的原因，也不知道决定来自算法。": "No feedback on why she didn't match; no way to tell if it was a genuine misfit or a parsing miss · No disclosure that an algorithm made the decision", "及时、坦诚地说明拒绝原因，让申请得到明确回应。": "Fast, honest rejections (with a hint of why) turn the black hole into prompt closure and preserve goodwill", "等了数周，只收到没有反馈的模板拒信。": "Form-letter rejection with no feedback after weeks of waiting", "及时、有人情味的回复，哪怕只提供少量个性化反馈。": "A timely, human, even slightly personalized rejection preserves goodwill", "始终没有结果，只能自己猜测已被拒绝。": "No closure ever; she's left to assume rejection", "岗位关闭时自动通知申请人，结束无期限的等待。": "An automatic \"the role is closed\" sweep costs nothing and eliminates this ending entirely", "LinkedIn / 招聘网站 / 企业招聘页": "LinkedIn / job board / careers page", "招聘门户（ATS）": "Careers portal (ATS-hosted)", "招聘门户": "Careers portal", "邮件": "Email", "自动筛选（用户不可见）": "Automated (no visible touchpoint for Maya)", "门户 → 邮件 → LinkedIn": "Portal, then email, then LinkedIn", "邮件通知，或没有回应": "Email (rejection or advance), or silence", "邮件 / 招聘人员来电": "Email / recruiter call", "情绪未记录 · 查看原始字段 ↗": "Emotion not recorded · View raw fields ↗", "故事": "Story", "快速开始": "Quick start", "安装 Skill": "Install the skill", "第一张旅程": "Your first journey", "持续使用": "Keep working", "修改与校验": "Edit and validate", "记录依据": "Record sources", "检查薄弱处": "Review gaps", "模板与主题": "Templates and themes", "字段参考": "Field reference", "实际示例 ↗": "Live examples ↗", "常见问题": "FAQ", "从第一段对话开始。": "Start with a conversation.", "Journey 是放在 coding agent 里的用户旅程 skill。你描述人的目标和遇到的问题，它帮助整理成一份能持续更新的地图。": "Journey is a customer journey skill for coding agents. Describe a person's goals and problems; it helps turn that understanding into a map you can keep updating.", "01　安装到你的环境": "01  Install in your environment", "需要 Git，以及能读取对应 skills 目录的 Claude Code 或 Codex。选择你的环境，把命令粘贴到终端执行。": "You need Git and Claude Code or Codex with access to its skills directory. Choose your environment and run the command in your terminal.", "安装后，在项目里开始一段关于用户体验的对话。": "After installation, open your project and start a conversation about the user experience.", "如果对应目录已经存在，请先检查现有安装。不要用新 clone 覆盖你已有的修改。安装后在目标项目中开启新会话，让 agent 读取 skill。": "If the target directory already exists, inspect the existing installation first. Keep any local changes. Then start a new conversation in your project so the agent can load the skill.", "02　讲清楚一个人的目标": "02  Describe one person's goal", "可以从现有访谈、产品说明或一段具体经历开始。无需先挑字段，也不必提前画完整流程。": "Start with an interview, a product description or a specific experience. You do not need to choose fields or draw the entire process first.", "没有真实资料时，也可以先建立草稿，但应当把假设保留下来，等后续观察来确认。": "You can start a draft without research, but keep assumptions explicit until observations can confirm them.", "03　找到留下来的地图": "03  Find the saved map", "旅程通常保存在项目的": "Journeys are usually saved in your project's", "目录中。检查 agent 回报的路径，确认文件已经写入。": "directory. Check the path reported by the agent to confirm that the file was written.", "它是你拥有的本地文件，可以放进版本控制。后续对话可以继续读取和修改这份旅程。": "It is a local file you own and can version. Later conversations can read and update the same journey.", "04　试着修改一次，再换个视角": "04  Make a change, then change the view", "你可以要求查看修改、检查缺少的依据，或把旅程表达为简报和工程交接。": "Ask to inspect changes, find missing evidence, or turn the journey into a brief or engineering handoff.", "看看一次实际的示例修改 ↗": "Explore an example change ↗", "需要先学会服务设计或字段名称吗？": "Do I need to learn service design or field names first?", "不需要。先讲清楚场景、人的目标和你掌握的信息，字段随需要出现。字段参考用于深入检查和自定义表达。": "No. Describe the situation, the person's goal and what you know. Fields emerge as needed. Use the reference for deeper inspection and custom outputs.", "地图保存在什么地方？": "Where is the map saved?", "本地项目中的 .journey/ 目录。无法写文件的环境可以在对话里返回内容，由你保存。具体位置应以 agent 的实际回报为准。": "In the local project's .journey/ directory. If the environment cannot write files, the agent can return the content for you to save. Check its actual report for the location.", "能自动证明某个需求是对的吗？": "Can it prove a requirement is right?", "不能。结构校验检查字段与引用，来源记录帮助追溯判断。真实体验仍然需要研究和验证。": "No. Validation checks structure and references; source records help trace judgments. Real experiences still require research and evaluation.", "可以用 Notion 或 Drive 多人同时编辑吗？": "Can several people edit at the same time in Notion or Drive?", "当前产品以个人在项目中持续维护理解为主。共享存储、多输入合并等团队能力仍在规划中。": "For now it is built for individual use: one person keeps their understanding up to date inside a project. Team features such as shared storage and merging multiple inputs are still planned.", "安装后还需要运行什么服务吗？": "Do I need to run a service after installation?", "Journey 不是独立的托管服务。它包含 skill 指令、模板和 shell 工具；写入、校验等脚本需要相应的 shell 环境，HTML 输出可在浏览器查看。": "Journey includes skill instructions, templates and shell tools. Writing and validation scripts need a shell environment; HTML outputs open in a browser. There is no hosted service to run.", "接下来": "Next", "持续更新这份理解 →": "Keep this understanding up to date →", "代码有地图，人的体验也该有一张。": "Your code has a map. So should the people using it.", "一份旅程。": "One journey.", "不同的表达。": "Different ways to express it.", "布局决定看什么，交互决定怎么读，主题决定呈现的色调。Journey 把这三件事分开，你可以重新组合。": "Layout determines what you see, interaction determines how you explore it, and theme sets the palette. Journey keeps these separate so you can combine them.", "模板是怎么做出来的？": "How are templates made?", "从旅程数据出发": "Start from journey data", "告诉 agent 读哪份 .journey/*.md、给谁看、希望对方做什么。已有字段决定内容，缺失信息保留为空。": "Tell the agent which .journey/*.md file to read, who the output is for and what they should do with it. Existing fields supply the content; missing information stays missing.", "组合布局与交互": "Combine layout and interaction", "agent 读取 rendering 模板的结构，再结合 interaction 模板的行为和 wireframe 参考，生成独立 HTML。模板可以按用途扩展。": "The agent combines a rendering template, interaction behaviour and wireframe references to produce standalone HTML. Templates can be extended for a particular purpose.", "用 theme 命令统一配色": "Apply colours with the theme command", "生成的组件使用语义颜色 token。theme 命令安装颜色体系，再用预设替换基础色，整张图自动派生。": "Generated components use semantic colour tokens. The theme command installs the token system and applies preset seed colours; the rest of the chart inherits them.", "选一种表达，拿走提示词。": "Choose an expression. Take the prompt.", "下面生成可交给 agent 的提示词与可在终端执行的命令。它不会在浏览器中运行 agent。": "This builds a prompt for your agent and a command for your terminal. It does not run an agent in the browser.", "01 / 布局模板": "01 / Layout template", "卡片图": "Card grid", "时间轴": "Timeline", "服务蓝图 / 泳道图": "Service blueprint / Swimlane", "情绪曲线": "Emotion curve", "覆盖矩阵": "Coverage matrix", "02 / 交互方式": "02 / Interaction", "布局参考 HTML ↓": "Layout reference HTML ↓", "交互参考 HTML ↓": "Interaction reference HTML ↓", "03 / 选择主题": "03 / Choose a theme", "Maya · 等待消息": "Maya · Waiting for news", "主题样张 / 摘录自同一份求职案例": "Theme sample / From the same job application example", "在完整地图中试用 ↗": "Try it in the full map ↗", "等待申请结果": "Wait for the application result", "−2 · 焦虑与失望": "−2 · Anxiety and disappointment", "展示审核进度与预计时间": "Show review progress and expected timing", "发送给 agent": "Send to your agent", "复制提示词": "Copy prompt", "Claude Code 使用 /journey 调用；Codex 可用 $journey 指定这个 skill。其余内容用自然语言描述。": "Use /journey in Claude Code or $journey in Codex to invoke the skill. Describe the rest in natural language.", "生成 HTML 后，执行换肤命令": "After generating HTML, run the theme command", "复制命令": "Copy command", "下载主题 CSS ↓": "Download theme CSS ↓", "将 map.html 换成实际输出文件名。命令会修改这个 HTML 的主题区域。": "Replace map.html with your output filename. The command modifies that HTML file's theme region.", "做成团队自己的 template。": "Make a template for your team.", "下载参考模板，放进项目的 templates/。定义布局、字段映射和交互，再让 agent 从这个模板生成下一张地图。": "Download a reference into your project's templates/ directory. Define its layout, field mappings and interactions, then ask your agent to use it for the next map.", "官网的传统「用户旅程图」也是定制布局：阶段为列、体验维度为行。它不是 skill 自带的某个同名预设；可以用相同的方法要求 agent 生成。": "This site's traditional journey map is also a custom layout: stages form columns and experience dimensions form rows. You can ask the agent to create one using the same approach.", "Skill 内置的布局参考。": "Layout references included with the skill.", "这些文件是 skill 的真实参考模板，包含占位或演示内容；下载后由 agent 替换为你的旅程数据。": "These are the skill's actual reference templates. They contain placeholders or examples for your agent to replace with your journey data.", "逐步阅读，按里程碑组织信息。": "Read step by step, grouped by milestone.", "沿时间顺序查看事件与等待。": "Follow events and waiting in time order.", "对照用户行为、前台、后台与支持层。": "Compare user actions, frontstage, backstage and support layers.", "观察情绪起伏与关键时刻。": "See emotional changes and critical moments.", "逐格呈现场景、动作、想法和时间。": "Show scenes, actions, thoughts and timing frame by frame.", "查看分支、循环与不同结局。": "Explore branches, loops and different outcomes.", "让时长与等待按实际数量呈现。": "Show durations and waits in proportion.", "检查字段密度、缺失与来源。": "Inspect field coverage, gaps and sources.", "来源：公开 skill 仓库快照 f30cc0b。": "Source: public skill repository snapshot f30cc0b.", "查看布局与交互组合规范 ↗": "Read the layout and interaction guide ↗", "哪些是命令，哪些是对话？": "Which parts are commands, and which are conversations?", "是确定性命令：安装 token、应用预设、设置基础色。生成布局和制作模板属于 Express 模式，由 agent 完成；目前没有": "is a deterministic command for installing tokens, applying presets and setting seed colours. Layout and template generation belong to Express mode and are handled by the agent. There is currently no", "或": "or", "命令。": "command.", "Graphite 是这个新版官网新增的主题文件，下载并安装后才能使用": "Graphite is a theme added for this site. Download and install it before using", "；其余四套预设来自当前 skill。": "; the other four presets come from the current skill.", "← 持续使用": "← Keep working", "在真实地图中试主题 →": "Try themes on the actual map →", "让理解，跟着项目走。": "Let understanding grow with the project.", "建立地图只是开始。需求变化时更新局部，交付时换一种表达，积累之后回头检查薄弱环节。": "Creating a map is the beginning. Update it as requirements change, choose an output for delivery, and revisit gaps as you learn.", "Plan · 建立第一份理解": "Plan · Build an initial understanding", "把目标拆成里程碑与步骤，再逐步加入行为、感受、触点和时间。优先保留能解释问题的信息。": "Break the goal into milestones and steps, then add actions, feelings, touchpoints and timing. Prioritise information that explains the problem.", "Modify · 改动局部，保留上下文": "Modify · Change a part, keep the context", "指出什么变了、为什么变。更新对应节点时，同时检查它与前后步骤的关系。": "Explain what changed and why. Update the relevant node and check its relationships with the surrounding steps.", "Validate · 写入前检查地图": "Validate · Check before writing", "确定性脚本检查结构与关联。删除一个仍被引用的步骤可能被拒绝，需要先修正引用。": "Deterministic scripts check structure and references. Removing a step that is still referenced may be rejected until the references are fixed.", "这段输出来自仓库的会议室运行记录。校验通过表示结构检查通过，不表示体验假设已经被证实。": "This output comes from the repository's meeting-room run log. Passing validation confirms the structure, not the experience hypothesis.", "Provenance · 保留判断的来处": "Provenance · Keep the source of a judgment", "来源标记区分模型生成、人工修改、引用依据和从其他字段合成的信息。它让后续对话能够追问，而不是把猜测越写越像事实。": "Provenance distinguishes model output, human edits, cited sources and composite information. Later conversations can question a judgment instead of treating a guess as a fact.", "示例中的来源属于案例设定。实际使用时，应记录真实、可核对的资料。": "Sources in this example are part of the scenario. In your own project, record real, verifiable material.", "Audit · 回看发生过的修改": "Audit · Review recorded changes", "通过脚本提交的变更会留下记录，包含作者、操作、目标和备注。直接手工编辑文件不等于经过同一条校验与记录路径。": "Changes committed through the scripts record the author, operation, target and note. Direct file edits do not go through the same validation and audit process.", "Review · 找出下一步该弄清楚的事": "Review · Find what to investigate next", "回看当前旅程里的弱点、信息缺口和相邻旅程。把需要补充的研究问题列出来，再决定下一步。": "Review weaknesses, missing information and neighbouring journeys. List the research questions before deciding what to do next.", "Express · 给不同的人，同一份理解": "Express · Share one understanding with different audiences", "可以输出故事线、一页简报、工程交接或交互 HTML。表达方式根据用途选择，原始旅程继续保留。": "Create a storyline, a one-page brief, an engineering handoff or interactive HTML. Choose the output for its audience while keeping the original journey.", "查看可操作的输出示例 ↗": "Explore interactive outputs ↗", "制作模板与设置主题 →": "Make templates and set themes →", "← 快速开始": "← Quick start", "字段参考 →": "Field reference →", "滚动阅读": "Scroll to read", "总览 + 局部": "Overview + detail", "缩放与平移": "Zoom and pan", "多视图切换": "Multiple views", "按里程碑分组，把每个步骤组织成可展开的卡片。": "Group steps by milestone in inspectable cards.", "时间轴保留事件顺序；需要比较真实时长时，选择时长比例图。": "A timeline preserves event order. Choose time to scale when comparing actual durations.", "用泳道区分用户、前台、后台和支持层，呈现交接关系。": "Separate user, frontstage, backstage and support layers to show handoffs.", "用 emotionValence 绘制情绪变化，未知值不补成零。": "Plot emotional changes from emotionValence. Unknown values are not zero.", "一格一步，映射场景、行为、想法、角色与时间，适合逐幕讲述。": "One frame per step, showing scenes, actions, thoughts, actors and timing.", "从 next 与分支条件建立连线，保留循环和多个结局。": "Build connections from next and branch conditions, retaining loops and multiple outcomes.", "按 duration / waitTime 编码实际时长；无法量化的值保留原文。": "Encode durations from duration / waitTime; retain unquantifiable values as text.", "呈现字段覆盖与来源标记，帮助作者发现空白与待验证的判断。": "Show field coverage and provenance to reveal gaps and judgments to verify.", "Graphite 是官网新增主题。先下载下方 CSS；默认从 Downloads 复制，保存到别处时请调整路径。": "Graphite was added for this site. Download the CSS below. The command assumes Downloads; adjust the path if you save it elsewhere.", "这是 skill 内置预设。下面按所选安装目录调用真实的 theme 命令。": "This preset is included with the skill. The command below uses the selected installation directory.", "# 先下载 graphite.css，再把它装进 skill 的主题目录": "# Download graphite.css, then install it in the skill's theme directory", "# 在 skill 目录下运行；map.html 指向你的输出文件": "# Run in the skill directory; map.html is your output file", "- _provenance: source: 走廊观察": "- _provenance: source: Hallway observation", "- momentOfTruth: 空房间就在眼前，却不能使用": "- momentOfTruth: The empty room is right there, but cannot be used", "└── onboarding.log   # 通过脚本写入的变更记录": "└── onboarding.log   # Changes committed through the scripts", "├── onboarding.md    # 里程碑、步骤和来源": "├── onboarding.md    # Milestones, steps and sources", "不要编造原始地图里没有的信息。": "Do not invent information missing from the original map.", "从用户的目标、行为和感受开始。": "Start from the user's goals, actions and feelings.", "使用 journey skill，帮我梳理新用户第一次使用产品的旅程。": "Use the journey skill to map a new user's first experience with the product.", "使用 journey skill，把 templates/storyboard.html 改成我们的评审模板：": "Use the journey skill to turn templates/storyboard.html into our review template:", "保留来源检查和键盘操作，所有颜色使用 Journey 语义 token。": "Keep source inspection and keyboard controls. Use Journey semantic tokens for all colours.", "先问我必要的问题；把已知事实和你的推断区分开。": "Ask me the necessary questions first. Separate known facts from your inferences.", "再给工程师一份交接，列出需要实现和确认的事项。": "Then create an engineering handoff listing what to implement and what to confirm.", "删除示例数据，留下字段映射说明，保存为 templates/team-review.html。": "Remove example data, keep field-mapping instructions, and save as templates/team-review.html.", "哪些失败情境没有恢复路径？接下来最值得梳理哪段旅程？": "Which failures lack a recovery path? Which journey should we explore next?", "帮我梳理用户从发现产品，到第一次完成核心任务的旅程。": "Map the user's journey from discovering the product to completing their first core task.", "我们现在允许用户跳过手机号验证。": "Users can now skip phone-number verification.", "把你不确定的地方标出来，先不要补成确定的结论。": "Mark uncertainties instead of turning them into firm conclusions.", "持续使用 · Journey Skill": "Keep working · Journey Skill", "文档 · Journey Skill": "Documentation · Journey Skill", "是谁改的？为什么修改？把相关记录列给我。": "Who changed them and why? List the relevant records.", "模板与主题 · Journey Skill": "Templates and themes · Journey Skill", "每一步显示行为、想法、触点、情绪、痛点与机会；": "Show actions, thoughts, touchpoints, emotions, pain points and opportunities at each step.", "然后把新旅程生成一个适合评审的交互地图。": "Then create an interactive map of the updated journey for review.", "给行政生成一页说明，强调规则变化和运营动作。": "Create a one-page brief for the admin team, highlighting rule changes and operational actions.", "请更新对应步骤，说明影响了哪些后续行动。": "Update the relevant steps and explain which later actions are affected.", "请检查这张地图：哪些关键时刻缺少依据？": "Review this map: which critical moments lack evidence?", "请移除提前预订步骤，修正关联引用，并列出这次修改。": "Remove the advance-booking step, fix related references and list the changes.", "这张旅程最近改过哪些步骤？": "Which steps in this journey changed recently?", "随后读取 .journey/job-application.md，基于它生成 review.html。": "Then read .journey/job-application.md and use it to generate review.html.", "预订现在变成可选了。": "Booking is now optional.", "Graphite · 石墨": "Graphite", "Paper · 纸白": "Paper", "Midnight · 午夜": "Midnight", "Blueprint · 蓝图": "Blueprint", "Contrast · 高对比": "Contrast", "情绪与认知": "Emotion / Cognition", "空间与渠道": "Physical / Spatial / Channel", "时间": "Time", "角色与协作": "People / Collaboration", "行动与行为": "Actions / Behaviour", "系统与技术": "Systems / Technology", "服务设计层": "Service Layers", "业务与指标": "Business / Metrics", "设计与机会": "Design / Opportunities", "失败与风险": "Failure / Risk", "路径与分支": "Paths / Branches", "沟通与内容": "Communication / Content", "无障碍与包容": "Accessibility / Inclusion", "搜索字段": "Search fields", "字段类别": "Field categories", "使用环境": "Agent environment", "模板主题": "Template theme", "安装环境": "Installation environment", "文件格式与规则 · Journey Skill": "File format and rules · Journey Skill", "文件格式与规则": "File format and rules", "命令参考": "Command reference", "一份 Markdown，": "One Markdown file.", "几条规则。": "A few rules.", "旅程地图是项目里的一份 Markdown 文件。agent 按这里的格式读写它，journey.sh 在写入前按这些规则检查。平时不需要手写，但知道它长什么样，更容易看懂每次修改。": "A journey map is a Markdown file in your project. The agent reads and writes it in this format, and journey.sh checks these rules before anything is written. You rarely write it by hand, but knowing its shape makes every change easier to read.", "文件与结构": "Files and structure", "每条旅程一个文件，放在项目的 .journey/ 目录里，文件名就是旅程的名字。通过脚本提交的修改，记在同名的 .log 文件里。": "Each journey is one file in your project's .journey/ directory, named after the journey. Changes committed through the script are recorded in a .log file with the same name.", "文件按顺序分三部分：": "A file has three parts, in this order:", "前言：用两行 --- 包住的旅程信息。": "Preamble: journey details between two --- lines.", "里程碑：二级标题，按旅程顺序排列。": "Milestones: level-two headings, in journey order.", "步骤：三级标题，写在所属里程碑下面。": "Steps: level-three headings under their milestone.", "一个完整的例子": "A complete example", "这个例子能通过 validate。": "This example passes validate.", "必填字段": "Required fields", "下面这些字段每份文件都要有。必填字段写在最前面，空一行后再写可选字段。": "Every file needs these fields. Write required fields first, then a blank line, then optional fields.", "位置": "Where", "记录什么": "What to record", "前言": "Preamble", "旅程的名称。": "The journey's name.", "创建日期，ISO 格式。": "Creation date, in ISO format.", "最后修改日期。通过脚本提交时自动更新。": "Date of the last change. Updated automatically when you commit through the script.", "参与者列表，每项包含 name、role 和 type。": "The people and systems involved, each with name, role and type.", "里程碑": "Milestone", "标题行。id 用 kebab-case，在文件内唯一。": "Heading line. The id is kebab-case and unique within the file.", "里程碑的名称和它涵盖的内容。": "The milestone's name and what it covers.", "步骤": "Step", "这一步有谁参与，写成数组。": "Who takes part in this step, as an array.", "这一步发生了什么。": "What happens in this step.", "personas 的 type": "Persona types", "含义": "Meaning", "这条旅程的主角。": "The main person whose journey this is.", "其他参与的人。": "Other people involved.", "自动化系统或机器人。": "Automated systems or bots.", "主角看不到的员工或团队。": "Staff or teams the main person doesn't see.", "前言里的可选字段": "Optional preamble fields", "可选": "Optional", "是": "Yes", "层级说明，默认是 Journey > Milestone > Step。": "Describes the hierarchy. Defaults to Journey > Milestone > Step.", "只主动建议哪些字段类别。不写就是自然模式。": "Which field categories the agent suggests. Leave it out for organic mode.", "自定义字段的登记表，每项带一句说明。": "The registry of custom fields, each with a one-line description.", "validate 会检查：前言的四个必填字段、每个步骤的 persona 和 description、id 是否为 kebab-case 且不重复、引用是否指向存在的步骤、字段名是否在 schema 里或已经登记。里程碑的 title 和 description 是格式要求，validate 不检查。": "validate checks the four required preamble fields, persona and description on every step, that ids are kebab-case and unique, that references point to existing steps, and that every field name is in the schema or registered. Milestone title and description are part of the format, but validate does not check them.", "字段的写法": "Writing field values", "每个字段是一行列表项：短横线、字段名、冒号、值。": "Each field is one list item: a dash, the field name, a colon and the value.", "简单值直接写在冒号后面。": "Simple values go straight after the colon.", "数组用方括号。": "Arrays use square brackets.", "嵌套值和同一字段的多条内容，用缩进的子项。": "Nested values, and several entries for one field, use indented sub-items.", "用 → 加步骤 id 引用另一个步骤。指向不存在的步骤会被 validate 拒绝。": "Refer to another step with → and its id. validate rejects a reference to a step that doesn't exist.", "可选字段共 93 个，分 13 类，见": "There are 93 optional fields in 13 categories. See the", "组合字段": "Composite fields", "有三个字段是对一组原子字段的概括。概括和细节说的是同一件事，所以同一个概念只填一层。": "Three fields summarise a group of atomic fields. The summary and the detail describe the same thing, so fill in only one level for each concept.", "汇总自": "Summarises", "两层都有时，以原子字段为准，组合字段由它们重新生成，并标上 auto-composite。": "If both levels exist, the atomic fields win. The composite is regenerated from them and marked auto-composite.", "只聊到概括层面时，可以只写组合字段。": "When the conversation stays high-level, the composite can stand on its own.", "agent 不会要求你在两层之间转换。": "The agent won't push you to convert between the two levels.", "schema 里没有里程碑级的组合字段。跨步骤的总结要么写成步骤上的组合字段，要么登记成自定义字段。": "There is no milestone-level composite in the schema. A summary across steps is either a composite on a step or a registered custom field.", "自定义字段": "Custom fields", "schema 里没有的概念，用带前缀的自定义字段记录，并登记在前言的 custom-fields 里。": "For concepts the schema doesn't cover, use a prefixed custom field and register it in the preamble's custom-fields.", "前缀": "Prefix", "用于": "Use for", "团队内部的概念": "Team-internal concepts", "行业特有的概念": "Industry-specific concepts", "假设与实验": "Hypotheses and experiments", "<自定>_": "<yours>_", "其他你自己定义的范围": "Any other scope you define", "agent 遇到新概念时，会先提议一个前缀，你确认后再登记。": "When a new concept comes up, the agent proposes a prefix and registers the field once you confirm.", "未登记的带前缀字段，validate 会拒绝。": "validate rejects a prefixed field that isn't registered.", "来源标记的四种状态": "Four provenance states", "来源标记记录一个字段的值从哪来。它是例外，不是常态：大多数字段不带标记，只有依据和人工锁定才会写。": "A provenance marker records where a field's value came from. It is the exception, not the rule: most fields carry none, and markers are written only for evidence and for values you have locked.", "状态": "State", "写法": "Written as", "模型生成": "Model-generated", "（不写）": "(nothing)", "默认状态。agent 根据对话写入，大多数字段都是这样，修改时可以直接更新。": "The default. The agent wrote it from the conversation, as with most fields, and may update it freely.", "人工修改": "User-modified", "你改过这个值，或明确要求按原话锁定。之后 agent 不会不问就改它。": "You changed this value or asked for its exact wording to be locked. The agent won't change it later without asking.", "有来源": "Source-based", "根据你作为依据提供的材料填写，例如访谈、数据或事故报告。": "Filled in from material you presented as evidence, such as interviews, analytics or an incident report.", "自动汇总": "Auto-composite", "由原子字段生成的组合字段。": "A composite field generated from atomic fields.", "标记写在它所标注的字段下一行，多缩进一级。缩进决定它属于哪个字段，嵌套字段也可以各带一个。": "Write the marker on the line below its field, one level deeper. Indentation decides which field it belongs to, and nested fields can each carry their own.", "没有缩进的 _provenance 会被 validate 拒绝。": "validate rejects an _provenance line that isn't indented.", "一个字段同一时间只有一种状态，以最新的为准。": "A field has one state at a time; the latest one wins.", "建图时 agent 不会逐条解释它写了哪些标记；修改时会读取标记，表达时会把它们呈现出来。": "While building a map the agent doesn't narrate its markers. It reads them when modifying and shows them when expressing the journey.", "类别激活": "Category activation", "可选字段分 13 类。默认是自然模式：前言里不写 active-categories，agent 按对话内容从任何类别建议字段。": "Optional fields fall into 13 categories. By default the map is in organic mode: with no active-categories in the preamble, the agent suggests fields from any category based on the conversation.", "记录了三到五个步骤后，如果一直在用同几类字段，agent 会问你要不要只关注这些类别。你同意后，它把这些类别写进前言。": "After three to five steps, if the same few categories keep coming up, the agent asks whether to focus on them. If you agree, it writes them into the preamble.", "你也可以一开始就指定。指定后，agent 优先从这些类别建议；其他类别的字段在你提到时照样可以写，只是不会被主动建议。": "You can also set them from the start. The agent then suggests fields from those categories first. Fields from other categories are still allowed when you bring them up; they just aren't suggested.", "journey.sh 是 skill 自带的 shell 脚本，只用 bash 和 awk。平时由 agent 调用，你也可以自己运行：在项目根目录执行，脚本路径指向安装好的 skill，例如：": "journey.sh is the shell script that ships with the skill; it needs only bash and awk. The agent normally runs it, but you can too: run it from your project root, pointing at the installed skill, for example:", "下表省略了 journey.sh 前缀。": "The tables below leave out the journey.sh prefix.", "命令": "Command", "作用": "Does", "说明": "Notes", "检查一条旅程": "Checks a journey", "通过时输出 OK 和步骤、里程碑数量；不通过时逐条列出 ERROR 和行号。": "Prints OK with step and milestone counts, or lists each ERROR with its line number.", "新建旅程": "Creates a journey", "agent 写好整份文件，也可以从 stdin 读入。先校验再写入，并记一条 create。同名旅程已存在时拒绝。": "The agent writes the whole file; stdin also works. It is validated before writing and logged as create. Refuses if a journey with that name exists.", "按条件找步骤": "Finds steps by condition", "在 .journey/ 里的所有旅程中查找。每行一个结果：旅程、步骤 id、原因。": "Searches every journey in .journey/. One result per line: journey, step id, reason.", "全文搜索": "Full-text search", "不区分大小写。输出旅程、步骤、行号和那一行的内容。": "Case-insensitive. Prints the journey, step, line number and the matching line.", "查看修改记录": "Shows the change log", "按时间排序，同一秒内的记录保持写入顺序。": "Sorted by time; entries from the same second keep the order they were written.", "查看修改署谁的名": "Shows who changes are attributed to", "依次取：set-author 保存的名字、git 的 user.name、系统用户名。来源是 fallback 时，agent 会问你一次该署什么名。": "Uses, in order: the name saved with set-author, git's user.name, then the OS user name. When the source is fallback, the agent asks you once what name to use.", "保存署名": "Saves the author name", "存在你自己的配置目录里（默认 ~/.config/journey-skill/author），不会写进旅程文件。": "Stored in your own config directory (default ~/.config/journey-skill/author), never in the journey files.", "给 HTML 输出配色": "Colours an HTML output", "见「模板与主题」。": "See Templates and themes.", "commit 的操作": "commit operations", "写法是 journey.sh commit <journey> <操作> [参数]。插入和替换用的块从 --block-file 或 stdin 读入。": "The form is journey.sh commit <journey> <operation> [args]. Blocks for insert and replace come from --block-file or stdin.", "操作": "Operation", "插入一个步骤": "Inserts a step", "也可以用 --before。块以": "--before also works. The block starts with", "开头，id 不能和已有步骤重复。": "and its id must not already exist.", "替换一个步骤": "Replaces a step", "值没变的顶层字段会保留原来的来源标记。": "Top-level fields whose value is unchanged keep their provenance markers.", "删除一个步骤": "Removes a step", "如果还有别的步骤引用它，删除后的文件不合规，会被拒绝。先改引用。": "If another step still refers to it, the result is invalid and the commit is rejected. Fix the references first.", "插入一个里程碑": "Inserts a milestone", "也可以用 --before，锚点是里程碑 id。块以": "--before also works; the anchor is a milestone id. The block starts with", "删除一个里程碑": "Removes a milestone", "连同它下面的所有步骤一起删除。": "Its steps are removed with it.", "登记自定义字段": "Registers a custom field", "写进前言的 custom-fields。": "Adds it to custom-fields in the preamble.", "每个 commit 都可以带 --note \"<原因>\" 和 --author \"<名字>\"。写入前会更新 last-modified 并校验整份文件；不通过就什么都不写。通过后记一条修改记录。": "Every commit accepts --note \"<reason>\" and --author \"<name>\". Before writing, it updates last-modified and validates the whole file; if that fails, nothing is written. If it passes, one log entry is added.", "query 的过滤条件": "query filters", "过滤条件": "Filter", "找出": "Finds", "有 failureMode 但没有 recoveryPath 的步骤。": "Steps with failureMode but no recoveryPath.", "有 momentOfTruth，但它没有 source 标记，步骤上也没有 metric、kpi 或 dropoffRate。": "Steps with momentOfTruth that has no source marker, on a step with no metric, kpi or dropoffRate.", "带人工修改标记的步骤。": "Steps with any user-modified marker.", "persona 里包含这个角色的步骤。": "Steps whose persona includes this name.", "有这个字段的步骤。": "Steps that have this field.", "缺这个字段的步骤。": "Steps that lack this field.", "修改记录": "Change log", "每条旅程旁边有一个同名的 .log 文件，每行一次修改，用制表符分隔：时间（UTC）、作者、旅程、操作、目标、备注。只有脚本会写它。": "Each journey has a .log file with the same name. Each line is one change, tab-separated: time (UTC), author, journey, operation, target and note. Only the script writes to it.", "环境变量": "Environment variables", "默认值": "Default", "用途": "Purpose", "旅程文件和修改记录所在的目录。": "Where journey files and change logs live.", "skill 自带的 references/journey.schema.md": "the skill's references/journey.schema.md", "校验用的字段表。": "The field list used for validation.", "set-author 保存署名的位置。": "Where set-author saves the name.", "已知限制": "Known limits", "只支持一个人写入。没有文件锁，两个 commit 同时改同一条旅程，可能丢掉其中一次修改。": "One writer at a time. There is no file lock, so two commits to the same journey at once can lose one of the changes.", "commit 不会自动改写 next。增删步骤后，前后步骤的引用由 agent 在块里写好；指向不存在步骤的引用会被 validate 拦下。": "commit never rewrites next. When steps are added or removed, the agent writes the neighbouring references in its blocks; validate stops any reference to a missing step.", "replace-step 只为值没变的顶层字段保留来源标记。嵌套字段的标记要由 agent 随块重写。": "replace-step keeps provenance only on unchanged top-level fields. The agent has to rewrite markers on nested fields in the block.", "直接手改文件不经过校验，也不会留下修改记录。改完可以运行一次 validate。": "Editing the file by hand skips validation and leaves no log entry. Run validate afterwards.", "query 和 search 每次实时读取文件，没有索引。": "query and search read the files each time; there is no index.", "没有 render 命令。HTML 由 agent 生成，theme 只负责配色。": "There is no render command. The agent generates HTML; theme handles colour only.", "脚本只处理本地文件。Notion 和 Drive 通过各自的 MCP 读写；没有存储时，agent 在对话里输出完整文件，由你保存。": "The script works on local files only. Notion and Drive are read and written through their MCP connectors; with no storage, the agent returns the full file in the conversation for you to save.", "← 模板与主题": "← Templates and themes", "名字必须是 <前缀>_<名称> 的形式。没有前缀的名字，register-field 会拒绝登记，并建议一个带前缀的写法；validate 也会把它当作未知字段拒绝。": "Names take the form <scope>_<name>. register-field refuses a name without a prefix and suggests a prefixed one; validate treats it as an unknown field too.", "开头，id 不能和已有里程碑重复。": "and its id must not already exist.", "写进前言的 custom-fields。名字必须带前缀。": "Adds it to custom-fields in the preamble. The name needs a prefix."};